1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,996
Spring Does Not Ask Permission

2
00:00:03,996 --> 00:00:31,040
Professor Azad Moradi’s notebook was full. He took out his lecture notes, the lecture he had meant to give on the morning of February 28: Kant’s Perpetual Peace. The backs were blank. No paper fit a war better. He wrote. The new leader’s name has been announced. A son. After forty-seven years we have come back to the same place. Only this time, a turban instead of a crown.

3
00:00:31,640 --> 00:00:59,716
History was not a circle. It was a spiral, passing the same place at a slightly different height each time. And on the spiral, spring came every year. Into the gunfire, into the black smoke. Spring did not ask permission. At that hour in Seoul, Kang Yujin fed hundreds of dots stalled in the Gulf into her model. The machine gave an answer. What could the people inside those dots be sure of tomorrow?

4
00:01:00,316 --> 00:01:04,056
Epic Fury continues in Episode 5.
